{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"secondary","scenes":[{"caption":"Friction opposes relative motion","duration_ms":9500,"id":"s1","narration":"A 60-newton push drives the block right while friction fights back with 40 newtons from the contact point. The net 20 newtons keep it sliding \u2014 friction opposes the relative slide, not the motion itself.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Friction fights the slide","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"floor","kind":"line","stroke":"#5d6d7e","width":5,"x1":80,"x2":880,"y1":400,"y2":400}},{"at_ms":700,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":120,"id":"block","explain":"The block: the object both forces act on.","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":140,"width":2,"x":160,"y":280}},{"at_ms":1200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"push","explain":"The push arrow: a 60-newton force driving the block to the right.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":40,"x2":140,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pushL","explain":"The push label: 60 newtons, the driving force.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"push 60 N","x":30,"y":315}},{"at_ms":1700,"do":"move","dur_ms":900,"target":"block","to":{"x":240}},{"at_ms":2900,"do":"move","dur_ms":900,"target":"block","to":{"x":320}},{"at_ms":4100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fric","explain":"The friction arrow: a 40-newton force opposing the slide, drawn from the contact point.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#2471a3","width":6,"x1":320,"x2":260,"y1":395,"y2":395}},{"at_ms":4400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fricL","explain":"The friction label: 40 newtons of friction. Smaller than the push, so the block keeps sliding.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"friction 40 N","x":140,"y":445}},{"at_ms":4700,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"fric","to":{"x2":200}},{"at_ms":5700,"do":"move","dur_ms":1200,"target":"block","to":{"x":400}},{"at_ms":5700,"do":"move","dur_ms":1200,"target":"fric","to":{"x1":400,"x2":280}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"verdict","kind":"text","size":26,"text":"Net force 20 N right \u2014 the block keeps sliding","x":80,"y":480}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"move","dur_ms":1500,"target":"block","to":{"x":480}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"move","dur_ms":1500,"target":"fric","to":{"x1":480,"x2":360}},{"at_ms":8900,"do":"caption","text":"Friction opposes relative motion \u2014 not always the motion."}]},{"caption":"Moments: force times distance from the pivot","duration_ms":10000,"id":"s2","narration":"Sixty newtons press down half a metre left of the pivot \u2014 a 30 newton-metre moment that tips the beam. Slide the 30-newton weight out to a full metre and its moment grows to 30 too \u2014 the beam levels as the moments match.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Balancing moments","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"M = F \\times d","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"beam","explain":"The beam: the rigid bar that tips or balances around the pivot.","kind":"line","stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":8,"x1":180,"x2":880,"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#5d6d7e","id":"pivot","explain":"The pivot: the fixed point the beam turns around.","kind":"polygon","points":[[530,344],[490,420],[570,420]],"stroke":"#2c3e50","width":3}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":80,"id":"weightL","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":80,"width":2,"x":430,"y":260}},{"at_ms":1750,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f1","explain":"The left force arrow: 60 newtons pressing down on the left side.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":470,"x2":470,"y1":190,"y2":255}},{"at_ms":2050,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f1L","explain":"The left force label: 60 newtons.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"60 N","x":488,"y":225}},{"at_ms":2250,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"d1","explain":"The left distance label: the force acts 0.5 metres from the pivot.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"0.5 m","x":400,"y":382}},{"at_ms":2450,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"mL","explain":"The left moment: 60 times 0.5 gives 30 newton-metres of turning effect.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"30 N\u00b7m","x":420,"y":155}},{"at_ms":2800,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":80,"id":"weightR","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":80,"width":2,"x":580,"y":260}},{"at_ms":3100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f2","explain":"The right force arrow: a 30-newton weight pressing down on the right side.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":6,"x1":620,"x2":620,"y1":190,"y2":255}},{"at_ms":3350,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"f2L","explain":"The right force label: 30 newtons.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"30 N","x":638,"y":225}},{"at_ms":3550,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"d2","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"0.75 m","x":585,"y":382}},{"at_ms":3750,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"mR","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"22.5 N\u00b7m","x":570,"y":155}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"beam","to":{"y1":385,"y2":295}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"weightL","to":{"y":268}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"weightR","to":{"y":249}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"f1","to":{"y1":198,"y2":263}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"f1L","to":{"y":233}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"f2","to":{"y1":175,"y2":240}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"move","dur_ms":1000,"target":"f2L","to":{"y":210}},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"verdict","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"60 \u00d7 0.5 = 30 beats 30 \u00d7 0.75 = 22.5 \u2014 left side tips down.","x":80,"y":480}},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"hide","target":"verdict"},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"hide","target":"d2"},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"hide","target":"mR"},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"d2b","explain":"The adjusted distance: the right weight slid out to a full metre from the pivot.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"1.0 m","x":615,"y":382}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"mRb","explain":"The new right moment: 30 times 1.0 gives 30 newton-metres, now equal to the left.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"30 N\u00b7m","x":600,"y":155}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"weightR","to":{"x":610,"y":260}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"f2","to":{"x1":650,"x2":650,"y1":190,"y2":255}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"f2L","to":{"x":668,"y":225}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"beam","to":{"y1":340,"y2":340}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"weightL","to":{"y":260}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"f1","to":{"y1":190,"y2":255}},{"at_ms":6100,"do":"move","dur_ms":1400,"target":"f1L","to":{"y":225}},{"at_ms":7800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"verdict2","explain":"The balance verdict: both moments are 30 newton-metres, so the beam stays level.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"30 N\u00b7m = 30 N\u00b7m \u2014 the beam is balanced.","x":80,"y":480}},{"at_ms":8700,"do":"caption","text":"Moment = force \u00d7 distance \u2014 slide the weight to balance."}]},{"caption":"Pressure: the same force on different areas","duration_ms":9500,"id":"s3","narration":"A 200-newton crate on its wide face presses 400 pascals into the floor. Tip it onto its narrow edge and the pressure arrows multiply: the same force over one-tenth the area makes 4000 pascals \u2014 watch the dent deepen.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Pressure = force over area","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"P = \\frac{F}{A}","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"floor","kind":"line","stroke":"#5d6d7e","width":5,"x1":80,"x2":880,"y1":420,"y2":420}},{"at_ms":1300,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#f0c27a","h":90,"id":"crate","explain":"The 200-newton crate: its weight presses down on the floor.","kind":"rect","stroke":"#8e5a2b","w":280,"width":2,"x":200,"y":330}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fArrow","explain":"The force arrow: the crate's full 200-newton weight pushing down.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":340,"x2":340,"y1":210,"y2":320}},{"at_ms":1700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fL","explain":"The force label: 200 newtons, the F in the pressure formula.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"200 N","x":368,"y":255}},{"at_ms":1900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"area1","explain":"The wide contact area: 0.5 square metres.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"A = 0.5 m\u00b2","x":200,"y":455}},{"at_ms":2300,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"pRead","explain":"The wide-face pressure reading: 400 pascals.","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"P = 400 Pa","x":560,"y":130}},{"at_ms":2700,"do":"show","shape":{"fill":"#a9cce3","h":8,"id":"dent","kind":"rect","w":280,"x":200,"y":420}},{"at_ms":3300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"crate","to":{"h":130,"w":180,"x":290,"y":290}},{"at_ms":3300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"fArrow","to":{"x1":380,"x2":380}},{"at_ms":3300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"fL","to":{"x":408}},{"at_ms":3300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"dent","to":{"w":180,"x":290}},{"at_ms":4300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"crate","to":{"h":180,"w":90,"x":335,"y":240}},{"at_ms":4300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"fArrow","to":{"y1":130,"y2":235}},{"at_ms":4300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"fL","to":{"y":165}},{"at_ms":4300,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"dent","to":{"w":90,"x":335}},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"hide","target":"fArrow"},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"hide","target":"fL"},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"hide","target":"area1"},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"hide","target":"pRead"},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"area2","explain":"The narrow contact area: 0.05 square metres, one tenth of the wide face.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"A = 0.05 m\u00b2","x":300,"y":455}},{"at_ms":5500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pa1","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":5,"x1":350,"x2":350,"y1":160,"y2":235}},{"at_ms":5750,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pa2","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":5,"x1":380,"x2":380,"y1":160,"y2":235}},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"pa3","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":5,"x1":410,"x2":410,"y1":160,"y2":235}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"pRead2","explain":"The narrow-edge pressure reading: 4000 pascals, ten times the pressure.","kind":"text","size":32,"text":"P = 4000 Pa","x":560,"y":130}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ratio","explain":"The rule in one line: one-tenth the area gives ten times the pressure.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Area \u00f710 \u2192 pressure \u00d710","x":560,"y":180}},{"at_ms":6800,"do":"move","dur_ms":800,"target":"dent","to":{"h":26}},{"at_ms":7800,"do":"caption","text":"Same force, smaller area \u2014 much bigger pressure."}]},{"caption":"Check the thinking","duration_ms":8000,"id":"s4","narration":"The trap says friction always opposes motion. Watch the driving wheel roll forward while its contact patch slides backward \u2014 friction pushes forward, driving the car.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Check the thinking","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"myth","kind":"text","size":28,"text":"Trap: friction always opposes motion.","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"road","kind":"line","stroke":"#5d6d7e","width":5,"x1":80,"x2":880,"y1":420,"y2":420}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":300,"cy":365,"fill":"#2c3e50","id":"wheel","explain":"The driving wheel: its contact patch pushes backward on the road as it rolls forward.","kind":"circle","r":55,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":3}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":300,"cy":414,"fill":"#f39c12","id":"chip","explain":"The marker chip on the tyre: it shows the wheel turning as the car moves.","kind":"circle","r":8}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"move","dur_ms":1500,"target":"wheel","to":{"cx":480}},{"at_ms":1400,"do":"move","dur_ms":1500,"target":"chip","to":{"cx":200}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tyre","explain":"The tyre push arrow: the tyre pushes back on the road.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#c0392b","width":6,"x1":480,"x2":380,"y1":414,"y2":414}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tyreL","explain":"The tyre-force label: the tyre pushes the road backward.","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"tyre pushes back on road","x":200,"y":455}},{"at_ms":4000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fr","explain":"The friction arrow: friction pushes the car forward, the road pushing back on the tyre.","kind":"arrow","stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":6,"x1":480,"x2":600,"y1":360,"y2":360}},{"at_ms":4200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"frL","explain":"The friction label: here friction drives the car forward, not backward.","kind":"text","size":22,"text":"friction pushes car forward","x":610,"y":368}},{"at_ms":5000,"do":"hide","target":"myth"},{"at_ms":5000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"fix","explain":"The corrected idea: friction opposes the relative slide between surfaces, not motion itself.","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"Friction opposes relative slide \u2014 not motion itself.","x":80,"y":505}},{"at_ms":6300,"do":"caption","text":"Contact slides back; friction drives the car forward."}]}],"subject":"science","title":"Forces: friction, moments and pressure","topic":"phys-forces"}